import ../../helpers/driver.dl

document reload test:
set instance to an instance of reload test
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 400 by 400 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
ignore update UI view the address of view
set surface to view's window as a pointer to test UI surface
reload UI image from (the string form of "image.webp") in (the address of view)
require condition (surface's image opens = 1) reporting "Reloading an uncached image started multiple requests"
set image to UI image from "image.webp" in (the address of view)
complete UI image image in (the address of view) with resource (7 as a pointer) sized 20 by 10 at status 1
reload UI image from (the string form of "image.webp") in (the address of view)
require condition ((image's status = 0) and (image's texture's resource = (0 as a pointer))) reporting "Reloading retained the previous texture"
require condition ((surface's image opens = 2) and (surface's image releases = 1)) reporting "Reloading did not release and replace the ready resource"
reload UI image from (the string form of "image.webp") in (the address of view)
require condition ((surface's image opens = 3) and (surface's image closes = 2)) reporting "Reloading a pending image did not cancel its request"
complete UI image image in (the address of view) with resource (0 as a pointer) sized 0 by 0 at status 2
reload UI image from (the string form of "image.webp") in (the address of view)
require condition (image's status = 0) reporting "An asset failure could not be retried"
require condition ((surface's image opens = 4) and (surface's image closes = 3)) reporting "Retrying a failed image did not release its previous request"
close the address of view
close the address of instance
print line "Image reload releases ready textures, cancels pending loads and retries failures."
